            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is already more or less possible with 'mini.hipatterns' by creating pattern for characters to cover and showing virtual text on top of them. There is even a [similar example in its help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c333187fcc76d7e772dac32c2a440a949fe34be4/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L158-L176).\r\n\r\nToggling should also possible in separate function, albeit not as straightforward: modify directly `MiniHipatterns.config.highlighters` to toggle certain highlighter (assign to table/`nil` to enable/disable) and follow by `vim.cmd('edit')` to \"restart\" all highlighters.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
